# NOVA - example environment file.
#
# Copy to `.env` for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY. `.env` is git-ignored.
# The production/supported path is the in-app Settings screen, which stores
# secrets in Windows Credential Manager (via keyring). Never commit real keys.
#
# Names are app-specific (NOVA_ prefixed) on purpose. An unrelated, unprefixed
# GEMINI_API_KEY exported by other software on this machine is IGNORED - it is
# never read. `nova diag` reports if such variables exist.
#
# Resolution order (first hit wins):
#   1. Windows Credential Manager (keyring)
#   2. this .env file
#   3. system environment variables
#
# Any value here is automatically registered with the log redactor and will
# never be written to log files, the audit log, or shown in the UI.

# --- Brain (Google Gemini) -------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey (format: AIza...)
NOVA_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Voice (ElevenLabs) ----------------------------------------------------
# https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys (format: sk_...)
NOVA_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# The voice to speak with (Voice Lab -> ID). Not secret, but kept here for dev.
NOVA_ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=

# --- Local development switches --------------------------------------------
# Environment label: development | production
NOVA_ENV=development
# Override the settings file location (optional).
# NOVA_CONFIG_FILE=
# Run fully portable: all data under ./.data (optional).
# NOVA_PORTABLE=1
